# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WORKING FILES — never commit. See CLAUDE.md, "THE REPO MUST BE PUBLIC".
#
# This repo is public because GitHub Pages only serves a public repo on the free
# plan, and that deploy IS the product. So the repo's contents are the only
# privacy control there is: only files the running app needs to build and serve
# may be committed. Everything below exists to support design, tagging or
# validation, and several of these carry real family names and real per-person
# food preferences. They live on disk, untracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# the tagged corpus and the scenario ground truth (real names + preferences)
meal-tags.json
scenarios.json
side-retag-RESULT.json

# the offline engine workspace: composeWeek, its adapter, the validation harness.
# At integration the engine's one app-required file moves into src/ — nothing here
# is ever committed from this path.
/engine/

# design, model and spec documents — handed between chats by James, not by git
MODEL-*.md
CONTRACT-*.md
HANDOFF.md
FACET-VOCABULARY.md
REFACTOR-for-engine.md
SPEC-*.md
CALENDAR-UPDATE-*.md
SIDE-RETAG-template.md
CORPUS-EDITS-*.md
BACKLOG.md
*-BRIEF-*.md
INTEGRATION-*.md
POST-INTEGRATION*.md
build-plan-page.js
*.pdf

# this working note (contains the pre-purge SHAs)
GITHUB-SUPPORT-REQUEST.md

# exported app databases (real names, preferences, notes) — the live DB lives in
